what claude did differently afaik:

*  all bad chars are encoded as `\x{...}`, even the C0 controls.
   (but this is fair; perl uses demarcating to disambiguate utf8
   strings from ordinary strings; deciding to go all-characters
   is a more consistent policy to follow.)
